    "title": "Offences relating to register of voters",
    "text": "Any person who — (a) by duress, including threats of any kind causes or induces any person or persons generally to refrain from registering as a voter or voters, or (b) in any way hinders another person from registering as a voter, commits an offence and is liable on conviction, to a fine not more than N500,000 or imprisonment for a term not more than five years.”",
