    "subsection": "3",
    "part": "Part IV — Procedure At Election",
    "title": "Format of ballot papers",
    "text": "The Commission shall, not later than 60 days to an election, invite in writing, a political party that nominated a candidate in the election to inspect its identity appearing on samples of relevant electoral materials proposed for the election and the political party may state in writing within two days of being so invited by the Commission that it approves or disapproves of its identity as it appears on the samples.",
