    "part": "Part V — Political Parties",
    "title": "Prohibition of use of force or violence during political campaign",
    "text": "A political party, candidate, aspirant, person or group of persons that contravenes the provisions of this section commits an offence and is liable on conviction — (a) in the case of a candidate, aspirant, or person or group of persons, to a maximum fine of ₦5,000,000 or imprisonment for a term of 12 months; and (b) in the case of a political party, to a fine of ₦10,000,000 in the first instance, and ₦2,000,000 for any subsequent offence.",
