    "section": "110",
    "subsection": "6",
    "part": "Part VI — Procedure For Election To Area Council",
    "title": "Election of Area Council Chairman",
    "text": "Where a candidate is not duly elected under this section, the Commission shall within 14 days of the result of the election held under this section arrange for another election between the two candidates and a candidate at such an election shall be deemed to have been duly elected to the office of a Chairman of the Area Council if he or she has — (a) a majority of the votes cast at the election; and (b) not less than one-quarter of the votes cast at the election in each of at least two-thirds of all the wards in the Area Council, as the case may be.",
